  "goodToKnow": "Der Täufer is a baptist: Johannes der Täufer (John the Baptist). In history, die Täufer were the radical Anabaptists of the Reformation, who rejected infant baptism; in 1534–35 they set up a short-lived kingdom in Münster, and the leaders' bodies were displayed in iron cages that still hang on the tower of St Lamberti. Mennonites and Amish descend from this movement. The plural is the same."
